WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:10.867
Building a property marketplace takes months. EstateHub is that marketplace, already built: the website, the seller portal, the admin console and the back end behind them.

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:18.798
Your visitors search on a live map. Every pin is a price, and every search is a link they can share.

00:00:19.898 --> 00:00:32.414
Or they just describe what they want. AI search turns one sentence into filters and shows the homes that match. It runs on OpenAI, Anthropic or Gemini, whichever you choose.

00:00:33.714 --> 00:00:39.510
When they find a home, they book a tour in a slot the seller has free, and reserve it by bank transfer.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:47.415
From then on, the deal is tracked stage by stage. Your buyer always knows what has been done and what comes next.

00:00:47.915 --> 00:00:52.303
They can compare homes side by side, and chat with the seller in real time.

00:00:53.903 --> 00:01:03.923
Sellers look after themselves. In their own portal they add listings, answer tour requests on a calendar, and see what each property has earned after your commission.

00:01:05.423 --> 00:01:07.848
Both portals come in light and in dark.

00:01:09.748 --> 00:01:25.059
You stay in control. Your team runs everything from one admin console. They approve listings one at a time, or a hundred in a batch. They verify identities. They work through each deal from a checklist. They confirm payments and send payouts.

00:01:26.759 --> 00:01:41.835
And it is yours to shape. Change the name, the logo and the brand colours from settings. Connect storage, email, sign-in and AI search from one screen. Even the steps of a deal are yours to edit. No code, and no rebuild.

00:01:43.135 --> 00:01:44.899
And all of it works on a phone.

00:01:47.199 --> 00:02:04.835
You get the full source of both sides: the Next.js front end and the Django back end. Django's own admin panel, a documented API, real-time chat and demo data come with it, so your developers can extend it, or build a mobile app on the same API.

00:02:06.735 --> 00:02:12.446
Launch sooner, under your own brand, on code you own. EstateHub. Start with it already built.
